! THE DECIMAL REFUSAL IS A MODEL SCOPE BOUNDARY, NOT IBM SEMANTICS, and
! this deck is labelled that way on purpose.
!
! The real 7030 performs decimal VFL arithmetic.  THIS MODEL DOES NOT,
! and refuses it with indicator OP (operation code invalid) so that an
! unimplemented operation is a VISIBLE refusal rather than a silent
! wrong answer -- the same choice bsv/README.md's scope list records for
! every other unbuilt operation.  What this deck pins is therefore the
! MODEL's documented boundary; it must not be read as a statement about
! the machine.
!
! The three RADIX CONVERSIONS are deliberately exempt and are tested
! elsewhere (decks/load_converted.strap, decks/vfl_convert.strap): for
! LCV, CV and LTRCV the decimal bit SELECTS A DIRECTION rather than
! asking for decimal arithmetic -- Reference Manual printed p.72, "If
! this bit is zero, the original field is binary; if this bit is one,
! the original field is decimal" -- so refusing them was refusing the
! operation's normal case.  See StretchExecute's `radixConv`.
!
! WHY IT NEEDED A DECK: it is one of the six causes of
! StretchIBox's prepareExec.completesWithoutFetch, and a census of which
! causes the corpus reaches (docs/ebox_roadmap.md) found this one and
! progressive-indexing-with-X0 firing ZERO times in 5621 checks.  Both
! were reasoned from the arms rather than measured.
!
! THE POSITIVE CONTROL IS THE POINT: the legal BINARY store runs first
! and its target is checked for the value it must have, so the deck
! cannot pass by doing nothing at all.
        SLC, (8)300.0
START   L(BU,32,8), DATA1
        ST(BU,32,8), TA+.48          ! legal: binary unsigned
        BOP, $                       ! hang if OP came on: that one is legal
        ST(DU,32,8), TB+.48          ! DECIMAL, and not a radix conversion
        BZOP, $                      ! hang if OP did NOT come on
        B, PASS
PASS    BEW, $
        CNOP
        SLC, (8)400.0
DATA1   DD(BU,32), (16)12345678
        SLC, (8)410.0
TA      DD(BU,64), (8)1777777777777777777777
        DD(BU,64), (8)1777777777777777777777
        SLC, (8)420.0
TB      DD(BU,64), (8)1777777777777777777777
        DD(BU,64), (8)1777777777777777777777
        END, START
